            {
              "text": "When selling an eight-figure ($10M+) luxury property on the Gold Coast, market reach, high-net-worth (HNW) buyer databases, and discreet negotiation skills matter far more than sheer volume. \n\nThe Gold Coast prestige market at this level is heavily dominated by two independent powerhouses, accompanied by a select group of major networks and specialist boutiques:\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Two Ultra-Prestige Market Leaders\n\n#### **Kollosche** (Led by Michael Kollosche)\n* **Reputation:** Widely regarded as the leading prestige agency on the Gold Coast by market volume and average sale price. They dominate sales above $10M, regularly transacting landmark estates and penthouses between $10M and $30M+.\n* **Key Suburbs / Strengths:** Mermaid Beach (Hedges & Albatross Avenues), Broadbeach Waters (Monaco Street), Isle of Capri, Surfers Paradise, and riverfront acreage.\n* **Why Consider Them:** They operate a collaborative, private-banking-style internal model where every agent shares buyer registries. Their marketing quality is award-winning, and their reach into wealthy Melbourne and Sydney buyers relocating to Southeast Queensland is virtually unmatched.\n* **Notable Agents:** Michael Kollosche, Troy Dowker, Sam Guo, Julia Kuo.\n\n#### **Amir Prestige Group** (Led by Amir Mian)\n* **Reputation:** The primary rival to Kollosche at the very top of the market. Amir Prestige is responsible for some of the highest recorded residential transactions in Queensland history (including several $20M–$28M sales along Hedges Avenue and Isle of Capri, as well as the $24M Glasshouse penthouse record in Burleigh Heads).\n* **Key Suburbs / Strengths:** Absolute beachfronts, mega-mansions on Sovereign Islands, Paradise Waters, Isle of Capri, and Mermaid Beach.\n* **Why Consider Them:** High-energy, elite marketing campaigns and massive quarterly prestige auction events (frequently held at The Langham). Amir maintains direct personal access to celebrity, interstate, and international ultra-high-net-worth individuals.\n* **Notable Agents:** Amir Mian, Carlie Mills.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Major Networks with Global & Interstate Reach\n\n#### **Queensland Sotheby’s International Realty**\n* **Reputation:** For trophy homes requiring exposure to cross-border capital (Asia-Pacific, North America, Europe) and wealthy southern-state buyers.\n* **Key Suburbs / Strengths:** Sanctuary Cove, Hope Island, Main Beach, and luxury gated estates.\n* **Why Consider Them:** The Sotheby’s global auction house affiliation provides institutional pedigree and marketing syndication across international luxury publications (Mansion Global, Wall Street Journal) that local independents cannot access directly.\n\n#### **Ray White Prestige (Surfers Paradise Group)**\n* **Led by:** Andrew Bell\n* **Reputation:** The largest real estate operation on the Gold Coast by scale. While they handle properties at all price points, their dedicated *Prestige Division* has decades of experience transacting eight-figure riverfront and beachfront holdings.\n* **Why Consider Them:** Unrivalled database size and their famous annual auction showcases (\"The Event\"), which generate intense international media coverage and competitive bidding environments.\n\n---\n\n### 3. High-Performing Boutique & Segment Specialists\n\n* **Coastal (Coastal Prestige / Tolemy Stevens):** If your property is a **luxury beachfront sky-home or sub-penthouse/penthouse**, Tolemy Stevens is widely considered the Gold Coast’s specialist for absolute beachfront apartment records (Broadbeach, Burleigh, Mermaid Beach).\n* **JW. Prestige Agents (Jordan Williams):** A long-standing boutique luxury specialist known for low-profile, off-market transactions of trophy waterfront estates and discrete high-end client representation.\n\n---\n\n### Recommended Next Steps for a $10M Listing\n\n1. **Shortlist by Micro-Location:** \n   * If **Mermaid Beach / Broadbeach Waters / Isle of Capri**: Interview **Kollosche** and **Amir Prestige**.\n   * If **Sovereign Islands / Sanctuary Cove / Hope Island**: Include **Amir Prestige** and **Queensland Sotheby's**.\n   * If a **Trophy Penthouse**: Include **Tolemy Stevens (Coastal)**.\n2. **Clarify Lead Representation:** In an eight-figure transaction, make sure the agency principal (e.g., Michael Kollosche or Amir Mian) or top partner is personally leading buyer negotiations, not handing the reins to junior associates.\n3. **Ask for Buyer Origin Data:** Ask the shortlisted agents where their last three $8M+ buyers originated (local upgrade, Sydney/Melbourne cash, or international) and what their specific strategy is to reach qualified, off-market buyers without publicly burning campaign days.",
              "thoughtSignature": ""
            }
